\label{cor:two}
By Lemma~\ref{lem:F}, $F>\sqrt p$ holds unconditionally and the only primes dividing $F$ are
$2,3$; hence the certificate needs at most the two witnesses $w_2,w_3$.

\label{cor:sieve}
In trial division up to $L$, only primes $q\equiv1\pmod3$ need be tested, i.e.\ half of the
primes in $[5,L]$ by Dirichlet.
